# What Cloudflare must NOT publish as part of the website.
#
# The built site lives at the repository root so that GitHub Pages can serve it
# too, which means the assets directory is the whole repo, and without this
# wrangler uploads all 3,308 files. That is how the first build failed: it hit
# node_modules/workerd/bin/workerd at 144 MiB against a 25 MiB per-asset limit.
#
# Patterns follow gitignore syntax, and the leading slash matters: a bare
# "*.js" would also exclude the site's own bundle under assets/.

# Editor and repo metadata.
#
# .git has to be here: the build clones the repository into the assets
# directory, so the pack file counts as an asset. It is what broke the second
# attempt, the same way node_modules broke the first, and it will only get
# bigger as history grows.
/.git/
/.gitignore
/.assetsignore
/.claude/
/.traycer/
/.wrangler/
/.gitattributes

# Toolchain and dependencies
/node_modules/
/site/
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/wrangler.jsonc
/.github/

# The research archive: source data, not the website. It stays in git and is
# published through the site's own pages rather than served raw.
/data/
/brand/
/backup/
/docs/
/_handoff_patches/

# Scraper and build scripts that live at the root
/*.js
/*.mjs

# Project documentation
/*.md

# Earlier generated pages, superseded by the site itself. Kept in git, not served.
/coldstream-*.html
/thumb-compare.png
